# Version bump on every change set

Whenever you make user-facing or packaged Aspera Dock changes that will be committed/pushed:

1. Check the latest GitHub release (`gh release list --limit 1`) and/or installed version.
2. Bump `package.json` `version` to the **next patch** (or minor/major if the change warrants it) **before or with** the commit.
3. Include the version bump in the same commit as the feature/fix when practical.
4. Mention the new version in the commit message (e.g. `Add downloads button (v0.1.9).`).
5. Push so CI can publish that release (Deploy workflow may also stamp from the latest tag — keep `package.json` ahead of or equal to the next expected release).

Do **not** leave `package.json` stuck on an old base version while shipping new builds.
